tadata: \u003cSENSITIVE, report disabled by configuration\u003e\n% git branch -a |cat\n* master\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -\u003e origin/master\n  remotes/origin/master\n```\n\nAfter uploading a small-ish binary file via the web UI, I can update the dataset without issues\n```\n% datalad update --merge\n[INFO   ] Fetching updates for \u003cDataset path=/tmp/datalad-test0\u003e \n[INFO   ] Applying updates to \u003cDataset path=/tmp/datalad-test0\u003e                              \nupdate(ok): . (dataset)\n```\n\nWhile the test file is checked directly into git, the repo is now an AnnexRepo (I assume the initial upload triggered that change on the server side):\n\n```\n% dl wtf -S dataset\n# WTF\n## dataset \n  - path: /tmp/datalad-test0\n  - repo: AnnexRepo\n  - metadata: \u003cSENSITIVE, report disabled by configuration\u003e\n```\n\nAdding a new file (actually the same file under a different name) and publishing it to GIN works nicely. The second file is annex'ed (although identical), so the decision annex or no for the initial upload must have been made by server-side logic and is not reflected in the dataset itself -- worth keeping in mind):\n\n```\n% git annex addurl https://der-roe.de/wp-content/uploads/final_testbild.png --file testfile2.png\naddurl https://der-roe.de/wp-content/uploads/final_testbild.png \n(to testfile2.png) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n% datalad save\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\n% dl status --annex all\n1 annex'd file (5.8 KB/5.8 KB present/total size)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/datalad-test0 (git)-[master] % datalad publish --to origin --transfer-data all\n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/tmp/datalad-test0\u003e data to origin \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/tmp/datalad-test0\u003e to origin \npublish(ok): . (dataset) [pushed to origin: ['[up to date]', '990cba7..f736bc4']]            \n```\n\nThe result of the upload is visible here https://gin.g-node.org/mih/datalad-test0/src/master/testfile2.png\n\nIt seems everything is nice and dandy.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1569055040,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzMzc3NzU0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2680#issuecomment-533777542"},"message":"Another scenario: Create an empty repo on GIN https://gin.g-node.org/mih/datalad-test1 and push an existing local dataset\n\n```\n% dl create test2\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test2 \ncreate(ok): /tmp/test2 (dataset)                                                             \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % cd test2\n\n% dl siblings add -s gin --url git@gin.g-node.org:/mih/datalad-test1.git\n[INFO   ] Failed to enable annex remote gin, could be a pure git or not accessible \n[WARNING] Failed to determine if gin carries annex. \n.: gin(-) [git@gin.g-node.org:/mih/datalad-test1.git (git)]\n\n% echo 123 \u003e dummy\n% datalad save\nadd(ok): dummy (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\ndl status --annex all\n1 annex'd file (4.0 B/4.0 B present/total size)\n\n% dl publish --to gin --transfer-data all \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/tmp/test2\u003e data to gin \npublish(ok): dummy (file)                                                                    \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/tmp/test2\u003e to gin \npublish(ok): . (dataset) [pushed to gin: ['f1ef9f1..da015a1', '[new branch]']]               \naction summary:\n  publish (ok: 2)\n\n% git annex fsck -f gin\nfsck dummy (checksum...) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n```\n\nFlawless.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1569055040,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI4MTQ0NzY0NA=="},"target":"d05973d410e625da8c0bef7b16e45d173995642d7db1dc13785eed391592dffa","message":"Another scenario: Create an empty repo on GIN https://gin.g-node.org/mih/datalad-test2 and push an existing local 